### Systemic sweeps beyond the quoted instances
- Unstable-vowel / mis-stemmed declension: 26 distinct tokens, 52 instances in total, replaced across
  columns-mn and the mn guidance region. On top of the reviewers' rows, a mechanical corpus scan
  (every word whose stem keeps a vowel that the same corpus drops elsewhere) surfaced four more of
  the same pattern, all fixed: 003 «тэтгэлгийн алдагдалыг» → «алдагдлыг», 003 «журамийн» → «журмын»,
  007 «эвлэрийн бүрдэлт/тэмдэглэл» → «эвлэрлийн …» (2 instances, stem is эвлэрэл).
  After the sweep the scan reports zero remaining same-word-two-spellings pairs.
- «аж ахуй» → «аж ахуйн нэгж»: 36 instances, entity sense only. NOT changed where «аж ахуй» is part
  of a Taiwanese tax name («аж ахуйн албан татвар» 營業稅, «ашгийн төлөөх аж ахуйн орлогын албан татвар»
  營利事業所得稅 — R8 wants one name per locale) or where it is the abstract undertaking rather than a legal
  person («аж ахуйн ашиг» business profits, «аж ахуйн зардал» business expense in 002, «аж ахуй, хөрөнгө
  шилжүүлэн авах» 營業讓與 in 017, «аж ахуйд хөрөнгө оруулах» in 016, «аж ахуйн байдлаас хамаарч» in 008).
- Country-name capitalisation: 8 instances (003 ×2, 004 ×1, 005 ×2, 006 ×3).
- Full stops on blog-register lines: 5 instances in 008.

## Rows skipped (with reason)
mn-a 21 and mn-b 22 — U+200B blank lines and the "make Q16–Q20 headings" half of mn-a 21.
  BLOCKED BY THE CHECKER, not by preference. scripts/check-column-translation.mjs compares the target's
  ZWSP count and its full heading-level array against the KOREAN SOURCE:
  checkBlocks → `if (sourceZwsp !== targetZwsp) details.push(...)`, checkHeadings → `JSON.stringify(sourceLevels) !== JSON.stringify(targetLevels)`.
  Measured source/target ZWSP counts are identical today (003 52/52, 005 8/8, 006 4/4, 008 10/10,
  009 5/5, 013 5/5, 015 3/3), and the Korean 003 keeps Q16–Q20 as body lines too. Removing a single
  ZWSP or promoting one line to `##` turns `blocks`/`headings` FAIL. This is a source-level defect and
  belongs in "Decisions for the user", not in a locale fix lane.
mn-a 39 — «TWD 1.57M» → «1,57 сая TWD». Skipped per ACCEPTED-ROUND: the string is in
  GUIDANCE_BIO_PRESERVED_TERMS (src/data/international-guidance-team.ts) and a test pins it byte-identical.
mn-a 40 — space thousands separators («1 000», «90 000») and code-after-amount. Skipped per
  ACCEPTED-ROUND / RULEBOOK R14: mn is in the comma-thousands group, the checker cannot parse space
  groups. mn-b's reviewer independently agreed and did not re-raise it. Row 42 was still applied, minus
  its number reformatting.
mn-a 1 (P1) — «10 дугаар зүйл» → «3 дугаар зүйл» in the 004 source list.
  APPLIED, THEN REVERTED because it breaks the numbers gate. Evidence (004 alone, after the change):
      numbers FAIL  missing from translation (1): 10
                    sourceCount=95 targetCount=94
                    [10] src="- [대만 법무부 법령정보 — 영업세법 제10조](…pcode=G0340028&flno=3)"
      summary FAIL 0/1 files
  The Korean source itself writes «영업세법 제10조» while linking flno=3, so the checker requires the digit
  10 in the translated label. Per the WO ("If the checker fails on a number/date, prefer the form the
  checker accepts and note it in the log") the label keeps «10 дугаар зүйл». The URL was never touched.
  The underlying mismatch is in the Korean original and needs a supervisor/attorney decision.

## Things I believe the reviewer got wrong (not applied)
1. mn-a 21 / mn-b 22 (U+200B and the Q16–Q20 heading promotion). Both reviewers read these as a
   Mongolian-side layout defect. They are inherited structure that the checker pins to the Korean
   source; fixing them in mn alone makes the file structurally non-isomorphic. See above for the exact
   failure mechanism. A fix has to start in src/content/columns/003 (and 005, 006, 008, 009, 013, 015).
2. mn-a 40 vs mn-b's verdict: the two reviewers disagree about the number format. mn-b explicitly
   accepts the code-first comma form ("that is the internationally used form and a Mongolia reader
   reads it without trouble, so I am not re-raising the earlier space-separator note"). The checker
   agrees with mn-b, so the corpus keeps the comma form.
3. mn-a 32's suggested wording, «нийтлэлийг … бүү тулгуурлаарай», is ungrammatical — тулгуурлах takes
   the dative, not the accusative. Only the imperative ending was changed; «нийтлэлд» stays.
4. mn-a 42's suggested wording moves the amounts to space groups; only the currency de-duplication was
   taken (see row 42 above).
5. mn-a 6's scope line ("runs through 001, 002, 004") undercounts on one side and overcounts on the
   other: 002's «аж ахуй» instances are all «аж ахуйн зардал»/«аж ахуйн албан татвар» (abstract/tax
   terms, correct as they stand and left alone), while 010, 015, 017 and 018 — which mn-b reviewed and
   did not flag — carry 28 genuine entity-sense instances. The sweep followed the pattern, not the
   file list.
6. mn-a 1 is right about the contradiction but the defect is in the Korean source (see skipped rows).

